{%- comment -%}
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   TESTING ONLY — staff J&T lookup.  REMOVE BEFORE PUBLISHING.
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Finds a customer's J&T shipments by phone, with the live scan history and
  the courier's Call / WhatsApp buttons, straight from OKA's J&T connector on
  GCP (jt-mcp-server) — to check the shipping connector on real orders from
  the website. The connector token comes from the test_connector_token
  setting (written into the page while the panel is on) or is typed in. Shown only when Theme settings → OKA order service →
  "J&T lookup panel" is on.

  To remove: delete this file, its render line in sections/oka-orders.liquid,
  the test_panel / test_connector_url / test_connector_token settings, and testLookup() in
  assets/oka-screens.js.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="test-panel" data-test-lookup data-default-url="{{ settings.test_connector_url | escape }}" data-default-token="{{ settings.test_connector_token | escape }}">
  <div class="test-badge">TESTING — staff only</div>
  <label class="field-label">J&amp;T connector address</label>
  <input class="field-input" data-tl-server type="url" dir="ltr" autocomplete="off" placeholder="https://jt-mcp-server-….run.app">
  <label class="field-label">Connector token</label>
  <input class="field-input" data-tl-key type="password" dir="ltr" autocomplete="off" placeholder="x-api-key">
  <label class="field-label">Customer phone</label>
  <input class="field-input" data-tl-phone type="tel" dir="ltr" autocomplete="off" placeholder="01X XXXX XXXX">
  <label class="field-label">Look back</label>
  <select class="field-input" data-tl-days>
    <option value="7">7 days</option>
    <option value="14">14 days</option>
    <option value="30" selected>30 days</option>
    <option value="60">60 days</option>
  </select>
  <div class="test-actions">
    <button class="cta bold" data-tl-go>Show shipments</button>
    <button class="outline-btn" data-tl-clear>Clear</button>
  </div>
  <div class="error-txt" data-tl-error hidden></div>
</div>
<div data-tl-results></div>
